{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC2 EVIDENCE (part 1 of 2) — runnable commands in docs/llm-framework.md \"Model providers\" section\n(lines 128-247 at origin/main d39bc122d7, i.e. the POST-merge text of d416ab9846), each EXECUTED.\nEnvironment: worktree /Users/joeoakhart/d129e-web-access, boto3/botocore 1.43.62, uv 0.9.x, py3.14.\n\n1. REGION MEASUREMENT — the doc's \"AWS_REGION alone does not resolve a region\" claim.\n   $ python -c \"import boto3; print(boto3.session.Session().region_name)\"\n   with AWS_REGION=us-east-1, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION unset, HOME=empty  -> None\n   with AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1, AWS_REGION unset              -> 'us-east-1'\n   Measured on boto3 1.43.62 / botocore 1.43.62 — the exact versions the doc names. CONFIRMED,\n   both arms, including the positive control.\n\n2. INFERENCE-PROFILE IDS — \"take every id verbatim from list-inference-profiles\".\n   $ aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --region us-east-1   (exit 0)\n   Returns, verbatim: us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 · us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 ·\n   us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0 (plus the global.* forms). All three ids the doc's\n   export block uses exist EXACTLY as written. The \"version suffixes are not uniform\" warning is\n   confirmed in the same output: haiku carries -20251001-v1:0 while opus/sonnet do not.\n   $ aws bedrock list-foundation-models --region us-east-1  -> lists NO us.* profile ids,\n   confirming \"list-foundation-models does not list profiles at all\".\n\n3. BARE ON-DEMAND ID MUST FAIL — executed as a REAL Bedrock InvokeModel:\n   $ boto3 bedrock-runtime invoke_model(modelId=\"anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\", ...)\n   -> ValidationException: \"Invocation of model ID anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 with on-demand\n      throughput isn't supported. Retry your request with the ID or ARN of an inference profile\n      that contains this model.\"\n   The documented error reproduced verbatim, from a live call — not by inspection.\n\n4. EXTRAS CONFLICT — \"[bedrock] declares a uv resolution conflict with [eval]\".\n   $ uv sync --extra bedrock --extra eval --dry-run   -> exit 2\n     error: Extras `bedrock` and `eval` are incompatible with the declared conflicts:\n            {`nava-rebar[bedrock]`, `nava-rebar[eval]`}\n   $ uv sync --extra agents --extra eval --dry-run    -> exit 0   (positive control: the pair the\n     pyproject comment says STAYS co-installable does)\n   PRECISION NOTE worth recording, not a doc defect: `uv pip install '.[bedrock,eval]'` exits 0,\n   because that path does single-platform resolution and does NOT honour [tool.uv] conflicts.\n   \"Not co-installable\" is true of the uv sync/lock (universal) path the conflict governs.\n\n5. INSTALL RECIPE — $ uv pip install --dry-run '.[agents,bedrock]'  -> exit 0, resolves.\n   $ python -c \"import pydantic_ai.providers.bedrock, boto3\"  -> BedrockProvider importable,\n   boto3 1.43.62 present, confirming the [bedrock] extra does pull pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock].\n\n6. PROVIDER SLIM GROUPS — \"a missing one raises a clear error naming the package\".\n   openai:  importable (OpenAIProvider) — [openai] group present.\n   google:  ImportError \"Please install the `google-genai` package to use the Google provider,\n            you can use the `google` optional group — pip install ...\" — a clear error that NAMES\n            the package, exactly as documented.\n\n7. PER-CLASS TOML SNIPPET — the documented [tool.rebar.llm.model_classes] block, written to a\n   scratch pyproject.toml and loaded through the real reader:\n   $ load_class_slots(root)\n     frontier -> ClassSlot(model='openai:gpt-4o', ...)\n     standard -> ClassSlot(model='google:gemini-2.5-pro', ...)\n     trivial  -> ClassSlot(model='local-model', provider='openai',\n                           endpoint='http://localhost:1234/v1', ...)\n   $ resolve_model_string('trivial', root) -> 'openai:local-model'\n   Parses and resolves as documented, including provider+endpoint composition.\n\nPart 2 (the local OpenAI-compatible server recipe and the per-class env-var invocations) follows\nin the next comment."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785821428566396001,"uuid":"de4b335c-ee0b-4739-8591-bb62557fdc4f"}